* Installation Guide

** Requirements

*** System Dependencies
    dotnvim requires the following system executables:
    - `dotnet` - .NET CLI (required)
    - `fd` - File finder utility (required)
    - `netcoredbg` - .NET Core debugger (optional, for debugging support)

*** Neovim Plugin Dependencies
    - `plenary.nvim` - Required for async jobs and utilities
    - `nvim-treesitter` - Required for syntax parsing
    - `telescope.nvim` - Optional, for project selection UI
    - `nui.nvim` - Optional, for bootstrap UI components
    - `nvim-dap` - Optional, for debugging support

** Installation Methods

*** Using lazy.nvim
    @code lua
    {
      'adamkali/dotnvim',
      dependencies = {
        'nvim-lua/plenary.nvim',
        'nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter',
        -- Optional dependencies
        'nvim-telescope/telescope.nvim',
        'MunifTanjim/nui.nvim',
        'mfussenegger/nvim-dap',
      },
      config = function()
        require('dotnvim').setup({
          -- Your configuration here
        })
      end,
    }
    @end

*** Using packer.nvim
    @code lua
    use {
      'adamkali/dotnvim',
      requires = {
        'nvim-lua/plenary.nvim',
        'nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter',
        -- Optional
        'nvim-telescope/telescope.nvim',
        'MunifTanjim/nui.nvim',
        'mfussenegger/nvim-dap',
      },
      config = function()
        require('dotnvim').setup()
      end
    }
    @end

*** Using vim-plug
    @code vim
    Plug 'nvim-lua/plenary.nvim'
    Plug 'nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter'
    " Optional dependencies
    Plug 'nvim-telescope/telescope.nvim'
    Plug 'MunifTanjim/nui.nvim'
    Plug 'mfussenegger/nvim-dap'
    
    Plug 'adamkali/dotnvim'
    @end

** System Setup

*** Installing .NET CLI
    **** Windows
         Download from {https://dotnet.microsoft.com/download}[Microsoft's official site]

    **** macOS
         @code bash
         brew install dotnet
         @end

    **** Linux (Ubuntu/Debian)
         @code bash
         wget https://packages.microsoft.com/config/ubuntu/20.04/packages-microsoft-prod.deb -O packages-microsoft-prod.deb
         sudo dpkg -i packages-microsoft-prod.deb
         rm packages-microsoft-prod.deb
         sudo apt update
         sudo apt install -y dotnet-sdk-8.0
         @end

*** Installing fd
    **** macOS
         @code bash
         brew install fd
         @end

    **** Linux
         @code bash
         # Ubuntu/Debian
         sudo apt install fd-find
         
         # Arch Linux
         sudo pacman -S fd
         @end

    **** Windows
         @code bash
         # Using chocolatey
         choco install fd
         
         # Using scoop
         scoop install fd
         @end

*** Installing netcoredbg (Optional)
    For debugging support, install netcoredbg:

    @code bash
    # Download the latest release from GitHub
    # https://github.com/Samsung/netcoredbg/releases
    
    # Or build from source
    git clone https://github.com/Samsung/netcoredbg
    cd netcoredbg
    mkdir build && cd build
    cmake .. -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr/local
    make && sudo make install
    @end

** Verification

   After installation, verify everything is working:

   @code vim
   :checkhealth dotnvim
   @end

   This will check all dependencies and provide guidance for any missing components.

** Basic Configuration

   Add this to your Neovim configuration:

   @code lua
   require('dotnvim').setup({
     builders = {
       build_output_callback = nil,
       https_launch_setting_always = true,
     },
     ui = {
       no_pretty_uis = false,
     },
     dap = {
       adapter = {
         type = 'executable',
         command = "netcoredbg",
         args = { '--interpreter=vscode' },
       }
     },
     tasks = {
       enabled = true,
       execution_mode = "dependency_aware",
       dap_integration = {
         enabled = true,
         block_on_failure = true,
         timeout_seconds = 300,
       }
     }
   })
   @end

